# netsurf + MacSurf bridge: ES modules load over the network
# Generated 2026-09-24
#
# claude.ai is a Vite app: one <script type="module"> whose static imports
# reach 66 modules (19 MB), and 2,600 more behind dynamic import(). MacSurf
# ran an external module as a classic script (SyntaxError at its first
# `import`), and its module loader knew only inline modules and the Mac's
# disk cache, so no import could load anywhere else.
#
# - script.c: type="module" scripts are flagged (html_script.is_module),
#   deferred unless async, and run by js_exec_module; inline modules are
#   deferred too (queued, run after the deferred scripts) and named after
#   the document so their relative imports resolve.
# - fetch_get_blocking() (content/fetch.h, curl.c): GET a set of URLs in
#   parallel (6 at once) on a private curl multi handle -- same user agent,
#   CA bundle, frontend name lookups, timeouts -- and wait for all of them.
#   QuickJS links a module graph synchronously, so its sources must be in
#   hand first. file: URLs are read directly (app0: pages' modules).
# - macsurf_qjs.c: js_exec_module scans the module's static imports
#   (`from "x"`, `import "x"`), fetches that level in parallel, scans those,
#   and so on (claude.ai: 65 modules, 3 levels, ~1 s on a desktop link);
#   the loader compiles each from that registry and frees its source, and
#   fetches a dynamic import() -- with its own static graph -- when it runs.
#   Specifiers resolve with nsurl_join (was: string splicing, so "/x" and
#   "../x" broke), and the normalized name is js_malloc'd as QuickJS frees
#   it with js_free. A module's evaluation promise is checked: a throw that
#   rejects it is logged with its stack (it used to pass as success).
# - The JS heap cap scales with the pointer size under
#   MACSURF_WINDOW_SERVICES: 128 MB on the Vita (of its 192 MB heap), 256 MB
#   in the 64-bit simulator. claude.ai's compiled app is ~99 MB there
#   (~60 MB on the Vita); at MacSurf's 96 MB every allocation failed and
#   QuickJS reported it as a bare `null`.
# testpages/pages/JS-module.html (with js-module-*.js): six checks, from app0:
# and over http in tools/run-vita-sim.sh.

